# Intent: Bench only. self.bench.mic3_check takes a slot (1 to 3) that changes the TDM slot read as the second channel at run time (the input is reopened); its answer names the slot. self.bench.firstrun {action done|reset} saves or erases the first-run record, so memory medians can be read with the first-run screen closed. The key exchange self-test answers its six-digit code as a string.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/boards/m5stack/core-s3/cores3_audio_codec.cc and .h (nested tree, MIT); firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: on a talkover image self.bench.mic3_check with slot 2 and slot 3 answers the slot used; self.bench.firstrun done answers ok and the first-run screen does not open after a restart.
# Kconfig: CONFIG_MAIPAI_SERIAL_TOOLS, CONFIG_MAIPAI_TALK_OVER, CONFIG_MAIPAI_LINK_PSK (existing)

